        <mxCell id="tmPk1bf3Kl_yN28Fl98g-11" value="&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;REC WIFI Wiring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The new REC WIFI module&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;will be wired as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;line-height: 70%;&quot;&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New harness Power line will be butt-spliced to existing wifi power&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New harness Ground line will be butt-spliced to existing wifi ground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 70%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Consider spade or bullet connectors instead of butt-splice to allow separation without cutting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillColor=#dae8fc;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3720" y="2299" width="540" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tmPk1bf3Kl_yN28Fl98g-13" value="&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;CAN Wiring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We need to check to see if we have a termination resistor at the REC BMS currently. I can&#39;t remember where else it is terminated in the existing system. &lt;/span&gt;Per the 1Q manual, it should be terminated in at the BMS via the REC CAN Cable&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does the CAN cable included in the 2Q Harness kit short pins 2 and 9?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillColor=#dae8fc;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2960" y="1270" width="1370" height="930" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
