        <mxCell id="EWNBWtAKwQsvnyJDCtDv-18" value="OPTOCOUPLE R1 COLLECTOR (IN) [OC 1 +]" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=22;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="655" y="3495" width="285" height="52.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EWNBWtAKwQsvnyJDCtDv-19" value="&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;I/O Wiring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; will be wired according to the table above and as follows using a 5.08mm pitch Phoenix connector to the left:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Existing wiring will be connected to a phoenix connector in the same configuration as the legacy BMS connector.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;IR SWITCH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; will connect to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;OPTO-RELAY IN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Pin 7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;IR PRECHG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; will connect to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;OPTO-RELAY OUT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Pin 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;CE TO OPTO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; will connect to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;OPTOCOUPLE R1 EMITTER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (i.e. out) which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Pin 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;CE FROM VBATT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; will connect to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;OPTOCOUPLE R1 COLLECTOR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (i.e. in) which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Pin 5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strike&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The output of the blue sea &quot;on switch&quot; will be split into three lines.&amp;nbsp; One line will go to the optocoupler board VBat+.&amp;nbsp; The other two lines will be butt-spliced to the lines for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Pins 5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strike&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The optocoupler board CHARGE ENABLE IN line will be butt-spliced to the l&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ine for Pin 1 of the &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;input/output prewire.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strike&gt;The REC Precharge BMS Input + line will be butt-spliced to the line for &lt;b&gt;Pin 3&lt;/b&gt; of the &lt;b&gt;input/output prewire&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/strike&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillColor=#dae8fc;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1520" y="3045" width="910" height="320" as="geometry" />
